 ## Overview
-The Two-stage CBR Method automatically generates transfer functions (TFs) for volume rendering by retrieving similar cases from a knowledge database of labeled volumes based on a user-selected ray's image and intensity profile features, then optimizing the retrieved TF for visibility [S1, unofficial][S2]. It sets itself apart from sibling methods like [Transfer Function Reconstruction Loss](1199-transfer-function-reconstruction-loss.md) or [AI-Based Transfer Function Peak Prediction](2921-ai-based-transfer-function-peak-prediction.md) by using a two-stage retrieval pipeline that combines deep spatial semantics (CNN) with local intensity profile matching (DTW) to identify Structures of Interest (SOIs), rather than optimizing a TF directly via gradient descent or predicting peaks [S1, unofficial][S2].
+The Two-stage CBR Method automatically generates transfer functions (TFs) for volume rendering by retrieving similar cases from a knowledge database of labeled volumes based on a user-selected ray's image and intensity profile features, then optimizing the retrieved TF for visibility [S1, unofficial][S2]. It sets itself apart from sibling methods like [Transfer Function Reconstruction Loss](1199-transfer-function-reconstruction-loss.md) or [Voxel-based Transfer Function Optimization](3259-voxel-based-transfer-function-optimization.md) by using a two-stage retrieval pipeline that combines deep spatial semantics (CNN) with local intensity profile matching (DTW) to identify Structures of Interest (SOIs), rather than optimizing a TF directly via gradient descent or predicting peaks [S1, unofficial][S2].
 
